1
00:00:48,950 --> 00:00:52,990
[The Old Story of Yu Hong]

2
00:00:53,360 --> 00:00:55,830
[Episode 24]

3
00:01:11,650 --> 00:01:13,760
Qianqian, which episode is on?

4
00:01:14,120 --> 00:01:15,830
Episode three.

5
00:01:16,210 --> 00:01:17,090
Episode three.

6
00:01:17,789 --> 00:01:19,450
What... is it about?

7
00:01:22,140 --> 00:01:23,450
Wh-What is it about?

8
00:01:24,350 --> 00:01:26,120
See for yourself.

9
00:01:27,080 --> 00:01:28,300
See for myself, huh?

10
00:01:32,039 --> 00:01:32,750
Juan.

11
00:01:33,640 --> 00:01:34,590
Back in our day,

12
00:01:35,039 --> 00:01:36,180
what did we watch?

13
00:01:36,780 --> 00:01:38,039
Just cartoons like...

14
00:01:38,450 --> 00:01:39,620
Havoc in Heaven,

15
00:01:40,370 --> 00:01:42,770
the Avanti series,
and other stuff, right?

16
00:01:42,979 --> 00:01:45,170
I can't hear the TV now.

17
00:01:46,009 --> 00:01:47,370
You can't hear the TV.

18
00:01:52,850 --> 00:01:53,509
Juan,

19
00:01:53,509 --> 00:01:54,160
you practically

20
00:01:54,160 --> 00:01:55,820
ordered an entire menu today.

21
00:01:56,289 --> 00:01:57,400
What? Are you still hungry?

22
00:01:57,400 --> 00:01:59,180
You're eating so many sunflower seeds.

23
00:01:59,180 --> 00:01:59,950
If necessary...

24
00:01:59,950 --> 00:02:02,280
m-maybe you should go to that diner again.

25
00:02:07,500 --> 00:02:08,530
J-Just tell me

26
00:02:09,340 --> 00:02:10,410
what you want to do with me.

27
00:02:10,410 --> 00:02:12,010
How else should I be punished

28
00:02:12,240 --> 00:02:13,710
to make you feel better?

29
00:02:15,940 --> 00:02:17,030
Go to bed, Qianqian.

30
00:02:17,030 --> 00:02:17,680
It's time.

31
00:02:21,870 --> 00:02:23,280
I'll tell you a story.

32
00:02:46,400 --> 00:02:47,460
What are you doing?

33
00:02:47,630 --> 00:02:50,030
Didn't you tell me to kowtow
and apologize?

34
00:02:53,430 --> 00:02:54,210
Move.

35
00:02:54,210 --> 00:02:55,130
Good dogs never stand in the way.

36
00:02:55,130 --> 00:02:56,200
Juan, Juan.

37
00:02:56,410 --> 00:02:58,090
I'm just feeling edgy.

38
00:02:58,090 --> 00:02:58,800
I've been here for days,

39
00:02:58,800 --> 00:03:00,090
yet there hasn't been a result.

40
00:03:00,090 --> 00:03:02,150
I thought I'd go back
after solving the case.

41
00:03:02,150 --> 00:03:03,750
Or it'd be too embarrassing.

42
00:03:05,210 --> 00:03:06,740
Are you that eager to leave?

43
00:03:07,060 --> 00:03:08,590
I'm eager to solve the case.

44
00:03:10,240 --> 00:03:11,770
But I don't think I'm wrong.

45
00:03:12,710 --> 00:03:13,970
You should leave soon.

46
00:03:14,280 --> 00:03:16,860
If not, even Qianqian will be
found suspicious.

47
00:03:16,860 --> 00:03:19,060
She arrived the day Zhao Changyou died.

48
00:03:21,060 --> 00:03:21,860
See, as I told you,

49
00:03:21,860 --> 00:03:23,790
this kid's way too clever.

50
00:03:23,810 --> 00:03:25,470
I should investigate her too.

51
00:03:25,870 --> 00:03:27,600
Why not investigate me as well?

52
00:03:28,410 --> 00:03:30,240
Where did Zhao Changyou lose his life?

53
00:03:30,240 --> 00:03:31,500
In my jurisdiction.

54
00:03:32,400 --> 00:03:33,530
Who was the witness?

55
00:03:33,750 --> 00:03:34,650
It was me.

56
00:03:34,840 --> 00:03:36,240
Such a coincidence, huh?

57
00:03:36,910 --> 00:03:37,960
Where did Li Dewu die?

58
00:03:37,960 --> 00:03:39,470
Also in my jurisdiction.

59
00:03:39,970 --> 00:03:41,250
So who's the biggest suspect?

60
00:03:41,250 --> 00:03:42,050
It's still me.

61
00:03:42,620 --> 00:03:43,520
I did both killings.

62
00:03:43,520 --> 00:03:44,190
You...

63
00:03:51,250 --> 00:03:51,750
I...

64
00:03:52,579 --> 00:03:56,040
My supervisor asked me to return
and report to him in a few days.

65
00:03:57,560 --> 00:03:58,760
Before my departure,

66
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:01,400
can you go look for clues with me?

67
00:05:08,510 --> 00:05:09,590
What do you want?

68
00:05:12,780 --> 00:05:13,660
To eat.

69
00:05:21,390 --> 00:05:23,190
Something just crossed my mind.

70
00:05:24,120 --> 00:05:25,000
Today, when I was

71
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:26,730
driving and passing No. 2 Road,

72
00:05:28,390 --> 00:05:29,870
a kid suddenly rushed out

73
00:05:29,870 --> 00:05:31,450
from the side of the road.

74
00:05:33,500 --> 00:05:34,830
Thank God I reacted fast

75
00:05:36,140 --> 00:05:37,740
enough to slam on the brakes.

76
00:05:38,920 --> 00:05:40,680
If I had hit the kid,

77
00:05:42,690 --> 00:05:45,090
he would've been terribly injured, right?

78
00:05:54,430 --> 00:05:56,630
Which kindergarten does your kid go to?

79
00:06:02,800 --> 00:06:04,200
No. 2 Road Kindergarten.

80
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:06,130
What a coincidence.

81
00:06:10,100 --> 00:06:11,120
When your child

82
00:06:11,120 --> 00:06:12,920
crosses No. 2 Road in the future,

83
00:06:13,370 --> 00:06:15,100
he had better be extra careful.

84
00:06:16,500 --> 00:06:17,920
Getting hit by a car

85
00:06:18,500 --> 00:06:19,560
is no small matter.

86
00:06:23,620 --> 00:06:24,420
Do you hear me?

87
00:06:28,220 --> 00:06:29,080
Yes, I hear you.

88
00:07:52,670 --> 00:08:01,440
[Platform 1]

89
00:08:15,540 --> 00:08:17,240
He Liang!

90
00:08:21,300 --> 00:08:23,160
He Liang!

91
00:08:27,040 --> 00:08:29,100
He Liang!

92
00:08:33,860 --> 00:08:34,549
Liang.

93
00:08:34,740 --> 00:08:42,159
[Platform 1]

94
00:08:36,049 --> 00:08:36,890
Why...

95
00:08:37,200 --> 00:08:39,470
Why did you leave without saying goodbye?

96
00:08:39,470 --> 00:08:41,750
That's not very nice.

97
00:08:41,750 --> 00:08:43,970
When will you be back?

98
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:46,790
When would you like me to be back?

99
00:08:46,790 --> 00:08:48,720
I don't know.

100
00:08:48,720 --> 00:08:51,460
You adults never keep your word.

101
00:08:51,460 --> 00:08:54,340
Dad said he'd pick me up in three months.

102
00:08:55,170 --> 00:08:56,830
I promise I'll come visit you.

103
00:08:57,390 --> 00:08:58,840
It's a deal then.

104
00:08:59,340 --> 00:09:02,820
Pinky swear. Once a word is given,

105
00:09:02,820 --> 00:09:04,680
-it must be kept.
-It must be kept.

106
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:08,110
He'll be back.

107
00:09:08,650 --> 00:09:09,770
Give me a smile now.

108
00:09:25,720 --> 00:09:26,980
Juan went out on a call.

109
00:09:27,250 --> 00:09:29,080
S-She's too busy to come here today.

110
00:09:29,080 --> 00:09:29,720
So,

111
00:09:29,720 --> 00:09:31,920
she had us bid you farewell in her stead.

112
00:10:28,570 --> 00:10:30,560
♪ Cold and warm, when can they rest? ♪

113
00:10:30,720 --> 00:10:31,850
Okay, you can go now.

114
00:10:32,850 --> 00:10:34,730
♪ Looking back, how many autumns? ♪

115
00:10:32,850 --> 00:10:34,230
How tall are you now?

116
00:10:35,990 --> 00:10:37,230
You're growing taller and taller.

117
00:10:36,420 --> 00:10:39,480
♪ Searched everywhere, yet lost instead ♪

118
00:10:37,550 --> 00:10:38,920
Let's watch Ikkyu-san.

119
00:10:40,210 --> 00:10:42,760
♪ What I didn't hope for is in my hand. ♪

120
00:10:44,060 --> 00:10:45,960
You've grown taller, Qianqian.

121
00:10:44,320 --> 00:10:46,370
♪ Did I get it or not? ♪

122
00:10:46,990 --> 00:10:50,230
♪ Can't explain the gains and losses,
the mistakes ♪

123
00:10:50,800 --> 00:10:54,790
♪ Just heard and saw, then it changed ♪

124
00:10:51,520 --> 00:10:52,940
Shake it. Get your body moving.

125
00:10:52,940 --> 00:10:53,800
Work your body.

126
00:10:54,170 --> 00:10:54,770
Shake it.

127
00:10:55,250 --> 00:10:59,000
♪ No idea where to trace it back ♪

128
00:10:56,960 --> 00:10:58,290
We are little gorillas.

129
00:11:00,170 --> 00:11:01,100
Take a look.

130
00:11:01,050 --> 00:11:03,830
♪ What do I seek in my whole life? ♪

131
00:11:01,100 --> 00:11:02,500
If you can't read it, just follow

132
00:11:02,500 --> 00:11:03,830
the phonetic spelling.

133
00:11:04,640 --> 00:11:07,950
♪ Always deciding
what to give up and what to hold ♪

134
00:11:05,210 --> 00:11:06,500
Do you know any swear words

135
00:11:06,500 --> 00:11:07,550
in Cantonese?

136
00:11:07,580 --> 00:11:08,840
The ruder, the better.

137
00:11:08,920 --> 00:11:09,950
Teach me a few.

138
00:11:09,390 --> 00:11:12,150
♪ I've worn out this life of mine ♪

139
00:11:09,980 --> 00:11:10,760
So I can curse her father out

140
00:11:10,760 --> 00:11:11,890
when I see him again.

141
00:11:12,140 --> 00:11:13,260
You have to be that mean?

142
00:11:12,210 --> 00:11:16,130
♪ Yet what I reach for
has already run away ♪

143
00:11:13,630 --> 00:11:14,550
Is that mean?

144
00:11:14,750 --> 00:11:16,230
What he did isn't exactly human, is it?

145
00:11:16,230 --> 00:11:19,390
♪ What do I seek in my whole life? ♪

146
00:11:20,010 --> 00:11:22,820
♪ In confusion, I can never
see it through ♪

147
00:11:24,750 --> 00:11:27,020
♪ I didn't expect what I lost ♪

148
00:11:27,770 --> 00:11:34,000
♪ Was already all I had ♪

149
00:11:40,930 --> 00:11:47,260
[Tiecheng Station]

150
00:12:07,270 --> 00:12:07,940
He Liang.

151
00:12:09,230 --> 00:12:11,570
♪ Cold and warm, when can they rest? ♪

152
00:12:10,420 --> 00:12:12,150
You couldn't be more careless.

153
00:12:12,930 --> 00:12:14,830
I can't believe you left behind
something so expensive.

154
00:12:13,090 --> 00:12:15,510
♪ Looking back, how many autumns? ♪

155
00:12:17,090 --> 00:12:20,260
♪ Searched everywhere, yet lost instead ♪

156
00:12:19,350 --> 00:12:20,350
I thought

157
00:12:20,530 --> 00:12:22,090
you wouldn't come see me off.

158
00:12:20,880 --> 00:12:23,210
♪ What I didn't hope for is in my hand. ♪

159
00:12:23,640 --> 00:12:25,290
You think I'm that petty?

160
00:12:24,850 --> 00:12:26,780
♪ Did I get it or not? ♪

161
00:12:26,770 --> 00:12:28,340
You left without saying goodbye.

162
00:12:27,630 --> 00:12:30,520
♪ Can't explain the gains and losses,
the mistakes ♪

163
00:12:28,740 --> 00:12:30,340
I hate it when people do that.

164
00:12:31,390 --> 00:12:35,340
♪ Just heard and saw, then it changed ♪

165
00:12:32,890 --> 00:12:34,950
You're just like Qianqian's father.

166
00:12:35,370 --> 00:12:36,660
How is that any way to behave?

167
00:12:35,490 --> 00:12:38,970
♪ No idea where to trace it back ♪

168
00:12:40,440 --> 00:12:42,090
You keep the recorder for now.

169
00:12:41,590 --> 00:12:44,000
♪ What do I seek in my whole life? ♪

170
00:12:42,650 --> 00:12:43,960
Just give it back to me

171
00:12:43,960 --> 00:12:44,760
when I return.

172
00:12:45,010 --> 00:12:48,080
♪ Always deciding
what to give up and what to hold ♪

173
00:12:46,070 --> 00:12:47,330
You will be back here?

174
00:12:49,960 --> 00:12:52,730
♪ I've worn out this life of mine ♪

175
00:12:52,880 --> 00:12:56,370
♪ Yet what I reach for
has already run away ♪

176
00:12:53,550 --> 00:12:54,610
That can't be true.

177
00:12:54,830 --> 00:12:55,440
You men

178
00:12:55,440 --> 00:12:56,940
always make empty promises.

179
00:12:56,900 --> 00:13:00,060
♪ What do I seek in my whole life? ♪

180
00:12:58,240 --> 00:12:59,960
I haven't solved the case yet.

181
00:12:59,980 --> 00:13:01,700
For the sake of that,
I'll have to come back here.

182
00:13:00,910 --> 00:13:03,330
♪ In confusion, I can never
see it through ♪

183
00:13:03,860 --> 00:13:04,460
Off you go.

184
00:13:04,580 --> 00:13:06,250
It's been a pleasure
spending these days with you.

185
00:13:05,120 --> 00:13:07,660
♪ I didn't expect what I lost ♪

186
00:13:08,340 --> 00:13:14,950
♪ Was already all I had ♪

187
00:13:09,250 --> 00:13:10,850
Just come back in five years.

188
00:13:33,630 --> 00:13:34,770
D-Don't leave a drop
in your glasses, guys.

189
00:13:34,770 --> 00:13:35,200
Quick.

190
00:13:35,200 --> 00:13:35,840
Drink up.

191
00:13:35,840 --> 00:13:36,500
Hey, Hong.

192
00:13:36,700 --> 00:13:37,320
Come on.

193
00:13:38,250 --> 00:13:39,390
Have one more drink with me.

194
00:13:39,390 --> 00:13:39,980
I can't, Mr. Lu.

195
00:13:39,980 --> 00:13:40,840
One last drink.

196
00:13:41,010 --> 00:13:42,120
I've had one too many.

197
00:13:42,120 --> 00:13:42,630
You drink with others.

198
00:13:42,630 --> 00:13:44,290
Just finish this one last cup.

199
00:13:44,770 --> 00:13:45,650
I propose

200
00:13:46,150 --> 00:13:47,530
that they drink in wedding style.

201
00:13:47,530 --> 00:13:49,050
Yes, in wedding style!

202
00:13:49,240 --> 00:13:49,950
Do it now!

203
00:13:50,370 --> 00:13:51,290
Drink in wedding style!

204
00:13:51,290 --> 00:13:53,660
You drink with him. I won't.

205
00:13:53,690 --> 00:13:54,940
-How am I supposed to do it alone?
-Mr. Lu.

206
00:13:54,940 --> 00:13:55,530
Mr. Lu!

207
00:13:55,860 --> 00:13:56,440
Mr. Lu.

208
00:13:58,080 --> 00:13:58,650
Mr. Lu.

209
00:13:58,820 --> 00:13:59,500
Mr. Lu.

210
00:13:59,630 --> 00:14:00,630
Here's the thing.

211
00:14:01,100 --> 00:14:03,240
Ms. Chen has an upset stomach today.

212
00:14:03,240 --> 00:14:04,700
I'll drink this up for her.

213
00:14:11,390 --> 00:14:13,370
Can someone else take one's place
in having a wedding-style drink?

214
00:14:13,370 --> 00:14:13,890
Fine.

215
00:14:15,120 --> 00:14:16,780
Let's play by the usual rules.

216
00:14:18,130 --> 00:14:20,660
For each drink you have for her,
take two more.

217
00:14:40,170 --> 00:14:41,830
He can really hold his liquor.

218
00:14:43,080 --> 00:14:44,440
Then let's keep going.

219
00:14:44,700 --> 00:14:46,230
Here, the submarine style.

220
00:14:52,650 --> 00:14:53,580
Drink up!

221
00:14:55,630 --> 00:14:56,960
Don't just stand there.

222
00:14:58,650 --> 00:14:59,840
H-Hey, you.

223
00:14:59,840 --> 00:15:00,340
Look...

224
00:15:00,790 --> 00:15:01,720
L-Lad, I am

225
00:15:01,720 --> 00:15:02,620
out of cigarettes.

226
00:15:02,620 --> 00:15:03,970
Go buy me a new pack.

227
00:15:04,220 --> 00:15:04,820
Off you go!

228
00:15:05,290 --> 00:15:05,990
Liu,

229
00:15:06,220 --> 00:15:07,290
Mr. Liang thinks

230
00:15:07,320 --> 00:15:08,630
you're being a nuisance now.

231
00:15:08,630 --> 00:15:09,870
With you standing in the way,

232
00:15:09,870 --> 00:15:12,110
Ms. Chen won't get to finish
that wedding-style drink.

233
00:15:12,110 --> 00:15:12,940
Right?

234
00:15:21,050 --> 00:15:21,980
Waitress!

235
00:15:25,460 --> 00:15:25,860
Hello.

236
00:15:25,860 --> 00:15:27,370
Buy two packs of State Express 555.

237
00:15:27,370 --> 00:15:29,370
You may keep the change. Thanks.

238
00:15:30,410 --> 00:15:32,270
Care a lot about your employee, don't you?

239
00:15:32,270 --> 00:15:33,580
Is he going to work overtime

240
00:15:33,580 --> 00:15:34,410
tonight?

241
00:15:34,410 --> 00:15:36,410
Like, practicing reverse parking?

242
00:15:42,440 --> 00:15:43,640
Reverse parking...

243
00:15:44,770 --> 00:15:46,910
It's not like that, Mr. Liang.
You must be joking.

244
00:15:46,910 --> 00:15:48,050
I'm just a driver.

245
00:15:48,050 --> 00:15:49,110
-Driver? No.
-I...

246
00:15:54,600 --> 00:15:57,000
Let me formally introduce him to everyone.

247
00:15:57,890 --> 00:15:58,820
This is Liu Yang,

248
00:15:59,080 --> 00:16:00,600
a proper graduate

249
00:16:00,600 --> 00:16:02,700
from the Railway Vocational College.

250
00:16:02,700 --> 00:16:05,440
He used to drive for me,
and that was purely transitional.

251
00:16:05,440 --> 00:16:07,030
Li's driver quit, didn't he?

252
00:16:07,030 --> 00:16:07,750
I couldn't find anyone smart

253
00:16:07,750 --> 00:16:09,790
to fill his position
within such a short time.

254
00:16:09,790 --> 00:16:11,720
So I had to make Liu settle for less.

255
00:16:12,200 --> 00:16:13,570
From now on,

256
00:16:13,770 --> 00:16:16,340
Liu is transferred
to a management position.

257
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:19,340
He'll be in charge of all orders
from outside the province.

258
00:16:19,340 --> 00:16:20,770
Contracts, too.

259
00:16:29,150 --> 00:16:30,880
What a mess we've created here.

260
00:16:30,990 --> 00:16:32,020
Yang, quick.

261
00:16:32,780 --> 00:16:34,440
Come on, a toast to Mr. Liu.

262
00:16:34,440 --> 00:16:35,200
-Guys.
-Here it goes.

263
00:16:35,200 --> 00:16:36,390
Mr. Liu, let me raise a toast to you.

264
00:16:36,390 --> 00:16:36,750
Come on.

265
00:16:36,750 --> 00:16:37,390
Let's drink together.

266
00:16:37,390 --> 00:16:37,820
Come on.

267
00:16:37,820 --> 00:16:38,790
-Mr. Liu, Mr. Liu.
-This is to you.

268
00:16:38,790 --> 00:16:39,320
Mr. Liu, here.

269
00:16:39,320 --> 00:16:40,130
A toast to you.

270
00:16:45,860 --> 00:16:46,520
Mr. Liang.

271
00:16:47,190 --> 00:16:49,180
You like smoking State Express 555, right?

272
00:16:49,180 --> 00:16:49,890
Listen.

273
00:16:49,890 --> 00:16:51,500
A friend of mine happens to be abroad.

274
00:16:51,500 --> 00:16:52,510
Next time he comes back,

275
00:16:52,510 --> 00:16:53,370
I'll have him bring some for you.

276
00:16:53,370 --> 00:16:54,790
And I'll personally deliver them to you.

277
00:16:54,790 --> 00:16:55,580
How about that?

278
00:16:55,580 --> 00:16:56,320
It's very kind of you.

279
00:16:56,320 --> 00:16:57,200
Thank you very much.

280
00:16:57,200 --> 00:16:58,600
N-No hassle for me at all.

281
00:17:01,080 --> 00:17:03,100
Actually, I think I've been smoking
too much

282
00:17:03,100 --> 00:17:04,000
lately.

283
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:05,400
It's like I'm addicted to it.

284
00:17:05,400 --> 00:17:07,060
I really should quit smoking.

285
00:17:07,980 --> 00:17:09,510
I'd like to propose a toast.

286
00:17:09,550 --> 00:17:11,810
Well, if there's anything
lacking in hospitality today,

287
00:17:11,810 --> 00:17:13,510
I hope you will forgive us.

288
00:17:14,380 --> 00:17:14,920
Not at all.

289
00:17:14,920 --> 00:17:15,880
Mr. Liu.

290
00:17:16,400 --> 00:17:16,810
That's not true.

291
00:17:16,810 --> 00:17:17,640
Please bear with us, everyone.

292
00:17:17,640 --> 00:17:18,160
A toast to Mr. Liu.

293
00:17:18,160 --> 00:17:19,030
Let's raise a toast to Mr. Liu.

294
00:17:19,030 --> 00:17:19,980
Mr. Liu, a toast to you.

295
00:17:19,980 --> 00:17:20,540
Mr. Lu.

296
00:17:21,630 --> 00:17:23,490
I'll drink this up, Mr. Lu.

297
00:17:24,900 --> 00:17:25,880
Let's not crowd up here.

298
00:17:25,880 --> 00:17:26,420
Go over there.

299
00:17:26,420 --> 00:17:28,280
Must have a drink with the beauty.

300
00:17:37,270 --> 00:17:38,670
The arm, the arm.

301
00:17:40,850 --> 00:17:42,070
Come on.

302
00:17:42,070 --> 00:17:44,310
Perfect time to practice reverse parking.

303
00:17:44,310 --> 00:17:45,600
Not a chance.

304
00:17:46,180 --> 00:17:47,710
What time do you think it is?

305
00:17:47,830 --> 00:17:48,960
I need to go home now.

306
00:17:51,180 --> 00:17:54,390
Can your wife promote you to manager?

307
00:17:55,180 --> 00:17:57,070
Or can she give you a child?

308
00:17:59,700 --> 00:18:01,140
With her poor health,

309
00:18:02,220 --> 00:18:04,480
is she even able to get intimate with you?

310
00:18:07,180 --> 00:18:08,580
We made a pact, didn't we?

311
00:18:09,700 --> 00:18:11,560
Things are better kept separate.

312
00:18:12,450 --> 00:18:14,390
You're leaving a soft, plump woman

313
00:18:15,270 --> 00:18:18,180
for that skinny one at home.

314
00:18:26,160 --> 00:18:28,920
For a while after Li Dewu died,

315
00:18:29,570 --> 00:18:31,400
I had nightmares every day.

316
00:18:32,880 --> 00:18:36,500
I dreamed that he chased and beat me
with that severed hand of his.

317
00:18:40,030 --> 00:18:42,160
But since I started sleeping with you,

318
00:18:43,380 --> 00:18:45,380
I've never dreamed about him again.

319
00:18:47,920 --> 00:18:50,680
I think I know why you married that girl.

320
00:18:51,550 --> 00:18:54,530
You believe that by making her your wife,

321
00:18:55,770 --> 00:18:58,030
all those things you did before

322
00:18:59,140 --> 00:19:01,660
can be wiped clean.

323
00:19:04,030 --> 00:19:05,360
Stop spewing nonsense.

324
00:19:06,880 --> 00:19:08,240
Nonsense?

325
00:19:10,380 --> 00:19:13,980
Nobody knows you better than I do,
Liu Yang.

326
00:19:15,350 --> 00:19:17,750
We're birds of a feather.

327
00:19:19,070 --> 00:19:22,000
Do you really think you can
instantly become a Buddha

328
00:19:22,640 --> 00:19:24,420
after laying down your knife?

329
00:19:27,420 --> 00:19:31,660
Who knows
what severe retribution awaits us?
